  <prompt>Owner-gated deploy + verify. Deploy the R4 code to dev with the BFF and the `sprk_spaarkeai` code page TOGETHER (advisory capability + per-Action opt-in + preference-producer on the BFF; SprkChatSuggestions gating + follow-on cards + D9 flex chain on the code page). Verify compressed publish size ≤60 MB with the delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline reported, no new HIGH CVE, new Action/Binding/tool catalog rows seeded, and the 7 spec Success Criteria DoDs exercised and ready for owner UAT. Confirm with the owner BEFORE each deploy; capture everything in notes/deploy-verify.md.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. BFF App Service + code-page deployment expertise; disciplined about the owner deploy gate, publish-size/CVE checks, catalog-row seeding, and post-deploy DoD verification.</role>
  <goal>R4 code is deployed to dev (BFF + sprk_spaarkeai code page together), compressed publish size ≤60 MB verified with the delta reported, no new HIGH CVE, the new catalog rows seeded, and the 7 spec Success Criteria DoDs exercised and ready for owner UAT.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Deploy + verify the whole R4 surface after all code tasks land (deps 013 advisory capability/BFF, 024 E2 follow-ons/suggestions, 033 E3 memory/preference, 040 D9 flex chain). BFF touches the ADR-039 projection + Action catalog + preference-producer; publish-size ceiling ≤60 MB (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs, 2026-07-08 — state the PDB convention when reporting). The BFF and the code page ship TOGETHER (the advisory capability's server side + the client suggestion-gating/cards/D9 fix are one release). Deploys are OWNER-GATED — confirm before each. New catalog rows (the advisory task-agenda Action + its Binding, the two Daily Briefing / Smart To Do surface-launch entries are code, but any Action/Binding/tool/`sprk_chiptransitions` rows must be seeded) go in via the seed scripts. Then exercise the 7 Success Criteria DoDs (P1 grounded-summary, advisory fidelity, P2 no-dead-end, follow-on cards, P3 preference loop, P4/D9 viewport, BFF hygiene) for owner UAT. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR (Services/Ai + ConversationPane + SprkChat heavily contended with compose-r5/r6 + assistant-r3).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (dotnet publish -c Release -o deploy/api-publish/ — measure compressed size + delta)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/ (build + deploy the code page — Deploy-SpaarkeAi.ps1 / code-page-deploy)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/ + scripts/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1 (seed any new Action/Binding/tool/chipTransition catalog rows)</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/code-page-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project" scope="deploy gate">Deploys are OWNER-GATED — confirm with the owner BEFORE deploying the BFF and BEFORE deploying the code page.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="ship-together">Deploy the BFF and the `sprk_spaarkeai` code page TOGETHER (the advisory capability's server + client halves are one release).</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="the BFF deploy">Compressed publish size ≤60 MB — measure + report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl. PDBs; state the PDB convention); ≥55 MB cumulative → architecture review; ≥60 MB → HARD STOP; ≥+5 MB single-task delta → justify.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02" scope="the BFF deploy">`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` shows no new HIGH-severity finding.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="catalog seeding">Seed any new Action/Binding/tool/`sprk_chiptransitions` catalog rows (byte-equal seed rows where D-4 parity tests guard) via the seed scripts — do NOT hand-edit prod rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="deploy skills">Use the bff-deploy + code-page-deploy skills; do NOT hand-roll deployment. Retry the code-page publish on transient 0x80071151.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
