  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm owner go-ahead to deploy. Run /conflict-check (Services/Ai + ConversationPane + SprkChat contended); re-sync origin/master into the branch and resolve any conflicts.</step>
    <step order="2">Build the BFF (dotnet build); dotnet publish -c Release -o deploy/api-publish/; measure compressed size; report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state PDB convention). HARD STOP if ≥60 MB.</step>
    <step order="3">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; confirm no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="4">Deploy the BFF via the bff-deploy skill (owner-confirmed).</step>
    <step order="5">Build the SpaarkeAi code page for production; deploy via Deploy-SpaarkeAi.ps1 / the code-page-deploy skill (owner-confirmed); retry on transient 0x80071151.</step>
    <step order="6">Seed any new Action/Binding/tool/chipTransition catalog rows via the seed scripts.</step>
    <step order="7">Exercise the 7 spec Success Criteria DoDs in the deployed env (P1 grounded cited summary + recommendation + Tasks opens; advisory fidelity/no second dispatch; P2 no dead-end + no id prompt; follow-on cards open/closed states; P3 preference loop; P4/D9 viewport; BFF hygiene).</step>
    <step order="8">Capture results in projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/notes/deploy-verify.md; note the owner UAT handoff; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If compressed publish size reaches ≥60 MB, or a new HIGH CVE appears, or the owner has not confirmed the deploy, STOP and escalate rather than deploying. If a single-task delta is ≥+5 MB, document the justification before proceeding.</trigger>
  </escalation>
